CHAPTER I GENERAL PROVISIONS

Article 1 (Purpose) The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters mandated by the Act on the Development and Management of Logistics Facilities and matters necessary for the enforcement thereof.

Article 2 (Scale of processing and assembly facilities) (1) The Facilities with a scale not exceeding the scale prescribed by Presidential Decree in the proviso to subparagraph 2 of Article 2 of the Act on the Development and Management of Logistics Facilities (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") means that the total floor area of a processing and assembly facility does not exceed 1/4 of the total floor area of a logistics terminal.
  (2) Other facilities prescribed by Presidential Decree, which have logistics functions in subparagraph 7i of Article 2 of the Act means the following facilities: <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Sep. 9, 2009; Dec. 14, 2009; Jul. 19, 2012; Mar. 23, 2013; Mar. 29, 2017; Feb. 19, 2021>
  1. A bonded warehouse under the Customs Act;
  2. Fishery Product Processing Business Facilities (limited to Freezing and Refrigeration Facilities) under Article 16 of the Seafood Industry Promotion and Support Act;
  3. A facility for loading, unloading, storing, or disposing of cargo within a harbor zone among harbor facilities defined in subparagraph 5 of Article 2 of the Harbor Act;
  4. A facility for the transportation of cargo and its auxiliary facilities and support facilities within an airport zone among airport facilities defined in subparagraph 7 of Article 2 of the Airport Facilities Act;
  5. A facility for the transportation, loading, unloading, or storage of cargo, which a railroad enterprise operator defined in subparagraph 8 of Article 2 of the Railroad Service Act uses for its business;
  6. Other facilities prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, among facilities for logistics;
  (3) Processing and manufacturing facilities prescribed by Presidential Decree in subparagraph 8a of Article 2 of the Act means the following facilities: <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Jul. 19, 2012; Mar. 23, 2013; Feb. 19, 2021>
  1. Deleted; <Feb. 2, 2012>
  2. Agricultural and Fishery Products Distribution Center under Article 51 of the Act on Distribution and Price Stabilization of Agricultural and Fishery Products (including a comprehensive livestock product disposal facility for slaughtering, processing, storing, etc. livestock products);
  3. Approval for matters, such as factories prescribed in subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Industrial Cluster Development and Factory Establishment Act;
  4. Factories producing processed marine products under Article 15 of the Seafood Industry Promotion and Support Act and marine product processing business facilities under Article 16 of that Act (excluding facilities for freezing and refrigeration business and facilities for onboard processing business);
  5. Other manufacturing or processing facilities prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.
  (4) "Facilities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in subparagraph 8e of Article 2 of the Act means the following facilities: <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Feb. 8, 2010; Mar. 23, 2013>
  1. Cultural and assembly facilities under subparagraph 5 of Appendix 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act;
  2. Facilities for disposal of wastes generated by tenant enterprises and support institutions (including recycling facilities);
  2-2. Facilities, such as detached housing, multi-family housing, etc. for the residence of employees and users of a logistics complex;
  3. Other facilities prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, among facilities to improve the function of logistics complex.

CHAPTER II ESTABLISHMENT OF COMPREHENSIVE PLANS FOR DEVELOPMENT OF LOGISTICS FACILITIES

Article 3 (Formulation of comprehensive plans for development of logistics facilities) (1) "Other matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 4(3)10 of the Act means matters concerning infrastructure, such as water supply, energy, and communications facilities.
  (2) "Where he or she intends to modify matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the latter part of Article 5(1) of the Act means where he or she intends to modify a plan for demand and supply of logistics facilities with at least 10/100 of the area of a site for each logistics facility for each logistics facility.
  (3) Where the head of the relevant central administrative agency requests the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport to amend a comprehensive plan for the development of logistics facilities pursuant to Article 5(3) of the Act, he or she shall submit documents concerning the following matters to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport: <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Mar. 23, 2013>
  1. Status of logistics facilities;
  2. Financing and investment plans;
  3. Other matters prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.
  (4) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport requests data or cooperation necessary for formulating or revising a comprehensive plan for the development of logistics facilities pursuant to Article 5(4) of the Act, the Minister shall clarify the details of such data or cooperation and the period for submission. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Mar. 23, 2013>

CHAPTER III LOGISTICS TERMINAL BUSINESS

Article 4 (Registration of complex logistics terminal business) (1) "Acts related to logistics prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 7(2)2 of the Act means the following Acts: <Amended on Jun. 26, 2009; Sep. 21, 2009>
  1. The Korea Railroad Corporation under the Korea Railroad Corporation Act;
  2. The Korea Land and Housing Corporation under the Korea Land and Housing Corporation Act;
  3. The Korea Expressway Corporation under the Korea Expressway Corporation Act;
  4. Deleted; <Sep. 21, 2009>
  5. The Korea Water Resources Corporation under the Korea Water Resources Corporation Act;
  6. The Korea Rural Community Corporation under the Korea Rural Community Corporation and Farmland Management Fund Act;
  7. The Port Authority under the Port Authority Act.
  (2) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 7(3) of the Act means matters other than the following:
  1. Alteration of the site area of a complex logistics terminal (only applicable to an alteration of less than 1/10 of the site area in total, notwithstanding the number of alterations);
  2. Alteration of the structure or equipment of the complex logistics terminal;
  3. Change of the name or location of the place of business.
  (3) Where a person who has filed for registration of complex logistics terminal business pursuant to Article 7(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "complex logistics terminal operator") intends to modify any registered matter pursuant to paragraph (3) of that Article, he or she shall file an application for registration of modification with the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, along with documents prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Mar. 23, 2013>

Article 5 (Authorization for implementation of projects) (1) Where a logistics terminal operator under Article 10(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "logistics terminal operator") intends to obtain authorization for the execution of construction works or authorization for modification thereto pursuant to Article 9(1) of the Act, the complex logistics terminal operator shall submit an application for authorization for the execution of construction works or authorization for modification thereto prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, along with a work plan, and a person who intends to operate general logistics terminal business shall submit it to the Special Metropolitan City Mayor, a Metropolitan City Mayor, a Special Self-Governing City Mayor, a Do Governor, or a Special Self-Governing Province Governor (hereinafter referred to as "Mayor/Do Governor") <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Mar. 23, 2013; Nov. 24, 2020>
  (2) Pursuant to the latter part of Article 9(1) of the Act, it is required to obtain approval for a revision to a construction plan, if the intended revision falls under any of the following cases: <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Mar. 23, 2013>
  1. Where the period of construction is changed;
  2. Where the site area of a logistics terminal is changed (limited to where at least 1/10 of the site area is changed);
  3. Where the total floor area of a building in a logistics terminal (referring to the total floor area of each floor of one building; hereinafter the same shall apply) is changed (limited to where at least 1/10 of the total floor area is changed);
  4. Where roads, railroads, squares, green areas, or other facilities prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport among public facilities in a logistics terminal are altered.

Article 5-2 (Scope of public institutions subject to special cases concerning expropriation and use of land) (1) "A public institution prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 10(1)2 of the Act means the following public institutions:
  1. The Korea Rural Community Corporation under the Korea Rural Community Corporation and Farmland Management Fund Act;
  2. The Korea Expressway Corporation under the Korea Expressway Corporation Act;
  3. The Korea Water Resources Corporation under the Korea Water Resources Corporation Act;
  4. The Korea Railroad Corporation under the Korea Railroad Corporation Act;
  5. The Korea Land and Housing Corporation under the Korea Land and Housing Corporation Act;
  6. The Port Authority under the Port Authority Act.
  (2) "Persons prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 10(1)3 of the Act means the following persons:
  1. Local government-invested public corporations prescribed in the Local Public Enterprises Act;
  2. Corporations established under any special Act.
  [This Article Added on Apr. 20, 2021]

Article 6 (Consultation on abolition of use) (1) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport or a Mayor/Do Governor intends to request the head of a relevant administrative agency to hold consultations on the disuse or sale of property owned by the State or a local government pursuant to the latter part of Article 13(2) of the Act, he or she shall attach the following documents: <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Dec. 31, 2008; Mar. 23, 2013>
  1. A detailed statement of the property subject to consultation;
  2. Documents stating the details of consultation on the abolition of use or sale, methods of appraisal of property, etc.;
  3. Deleted; <Dec. 31, 2008>
  4. Deleted; <Dec. 31, 2008>
  5. Location map;
  6. A certificate of non-registration (to be attached only in cases of unregistered property).
  (2) Upon receipt of a request for consultation under paragraph (1), the head of the relevant administrative agency shall verify the following administrative information by sharing administrative information under Article 36(1) of the Electronic Government Act: <Added on Dec. 31, 2008; May 4, 2010>
  1. A certified copy of the land register;
  2. A certified copy of the register;
  3. A certified copy of the land registration map.
  (3) The Minister of Finance and Economy may delegate the management or disposal of property managed or disposed of in accordance with Article 13(4) of the Act, in accordance with Article 42(1) of the State Property Act. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Dec. 31, 2008; Jul. 27, 2009; Dec. 30, 2025>

Article 7 (Criteria for imposition of penalty surcharges on complex logistics terminal operators) The standards for imposition of penalty surcharges such as their amounts under Article 18(1) of the Act, which vary depending on the types and severity of violations, shall be prescribed in Appendix 1.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jul. 19, 2022]

Article 8 (Imposition and payment of penalty surcharges) (1) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport intends to impose a penalty surcharge pursuant to Article 18(1) of the Act, he or she shall investigate and verify the relevant violation and notify the person subject to the imposition of the penalty surcharge of the payment thereof, specifying the fact of the violation, the method and period for raising an objection, etc. in writing. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Mar. 23, 2013; Jul. 19, 2022>
  (2) Any person in receipt of notification under paragraph (1) shall pay the penalty surcharge to a collecting agency designated by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport within 20 days from the date of receipt of such notification. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Mar. 23, 2013; Jul. 19, 2022>
  (3) A receiving agency in receipt of a penalty surcharge pursuant to paragraph (2) shall issue a penalty surcharge receipt to the person who has paid the penalty surcharge.
  (4) Where the receiving agency of penalty surcharges issues a receipt of penalty surcharges under paragraph (3), it shall send a notice of receipt to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Mar. 23, 2013>
  (5) Deleted. <Sep. 24, 2021>

Article 9 (Demand for payment of penalty surcharges and collection thereof) (1) Where a person in receipt of a notice of payment of a penalty surcharge pursuant to Article 18(3) of the Act fails to pay the penalty surcharge by the deadline for payment, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall send a reminder within seven days from the date on which the deadline for payment expires. In such cases, the deadline for payment shall be within ten days from the date on which the reminder is sent. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Mar. 23, 2013>
  (2) Where a person in receipt of a demand notice under paragraph (1) fails to pay a penalty surcharge by the payment deadline, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may require a public official under his or her jurisdiction to compulsorily collect the penalty surcharge in the same manner as national taxes are compulsorily collected. In such cases, the public official under his or her jurisdiction shall carry a certificate indicating his or her authority and present it to interested persons. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Mar. 23, 2013; Jul. 19, 2022>

Article 10 (Establishment of Association) Where a logistics terminal operator intends to establish the Association of Logistics Terminal Business under Article 19 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Association"), at least 7 promoters shall submit an application for authorization for establishment to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, accompanied by the following documents, following a resolution by the inaugural general meeting: <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Mar. 23, 2013; Apr. 7, 2026>
  1. Articles of association;
  2. A list and curricula vitae of the promoters;
  3. A list of members;
  4. A business plan and a plan on the revenue and expenditure of budget;
  5. Minutes of the inaugural general meeting.

Article 11 (Article of association) The articles of association of the Association shall include:
  1. Objectives;
  2. Name;
  3. Location of office;
  4. Matters regarding members and general meetings;
  5. Matters regarding executive officers;
  6. Matters regarding its affairs;
  7. Matters regarding accounting and membership fees;
  8. Matters regarding amendment of the articles of association;
  9. Matters regarding dissolution;
  10. Matters concerning the methods of making public announcement.

Article 12 (Business affairs) The Association shall perform the following business: <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Mar. 23, 2013>
  1. Projects to promote a sound development of the logistics terminal business and common interests of the relevant business operators;
  2. Research and development projects to prepare and manage statistics and to collect, examine, and research foreign data necessary for the promotion and development of the logistics terminal business;
  3. Education and training of managers and employees;
  4. Guidance on management improvement of logistics terminal business;
  5. Business activities entrusted by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport;
  6. Business incidental to those listed in subparagraphs 1 through 5.

Article 12-2 (Infrastructure) "Infrastructure prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as roads, railroads, and water supply facilities" in Article 20(2) of the Act means any of the following facilities: <Amended on Jul. 14, 2014; Jan. 16, 2018>
  1. Roads defined in subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Road Act;
  2. Railroads under subparagraph 1 of Article 3 of the Framework Act on Railroad Industry Development;
  3. Waterworks facilities under subparagraph 17 of Article 3 of the Water Supply and Waterworks Installation Act;
  4. Water pollution prevention facilities under subparagraph 12 of Article 2 of the Water Environment Conservation Act.
  [This Article Added on Nov. 27, 2012]
  [Previous Article 12-2 moved to Article 12-3 <Nov. 27, 2012>]

CHAPTER III-2 LOGISTICS WAREHOUSING BUSINESS

Article 12-3 (Registration of modification of logistics warehousing business) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso of Article 21-2(2) of the Act means any of the following matters:
  1. Name (in cases of a corporation, the name of its representative) and trade name of a person who has registered logistics warehousing business pursuant to Article 21-2(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "logistics warehousing business operator");
  2. Location of the logistics warehouse;
  3. Increase or decrease by at least 10/100 of the area of a logistics warehouse.
  [This Article Added on Feb. 2, 2012]
  [Moved from Article 12-2 <Nov. 27, 2012>]

Article 12-4 (Revocation of certification of smart logistics center) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport revokes certification pursuant to Article 21-5(1) of the Act, he or she shall publicly notify such revocation in the Official Gazette.
  [This Article Added on Oct. 8, 2020]

Article 12-5 (Support for smart logistics centers) (1) The State or a local government may provide the following support under Article 21-7 (2) of the Act: <Amended on Mar. 25, 2025>
  1. Partial subsidies or loans for expenses incurred in establishing a smart logistics center;
  2. The difference between the interest rate and the interest rate determined by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport in consultation with the head of the relevant central administrative agency, where a person who has obtained certification of a smart logistics center borrows a loan from a domestic financial institution to raise funds necessary for the establishment and operation of the smart logistics center; compensation for all or part of the difference;
  3. Application of the floor area ratio and the upper limit of height prescribed by ordinance of the Special Metropolitan City, Metropolitan City, Special Self-Governing City, Special Self-Governing Province, Special Self-Governing Province, or Si/Gun pursuant to Article 78 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act to the construction, expansion, or renovation of a smart logistics center.
  4. Other support provided by local governments, as prescribed by ordinance of the relevant local government regarding the revitalization of smart logistics centers.
  (2) The Korea Credit Guarantee Fund established under the Credit Guarantee Fund Act and the Korea Technology Finance Corporation established under the Korea Technology Finance Corporation Act may give preferential treatment to the conditions of guarantee, such as the limit of guarantee, guarantee fees, etc. for monetary liabilities arising from loans, etc. of funds necessary for the establishment and operation of smart logistics centers pursuant to Article 21-7(2) of the Act.
  [This Article Added on Oct. 8, 2020]

Article 12-6 (Standards for imposition of penalty surcharges on logistics warehousing business entities) The standards for imposition of penalty surcharges such as their amounts under Article 21-9(1) of the Act, which vary depending on the types and severity of violations, shall be prescribed in Appendix 1.
  [This Article Added on Jul. 19, 2022]

Article 12-7 (Imposition and payment of penalty surcharges) `Article 8 and 9 shall apply mutatis mutandis to the imposition, payment, etc. of penalty surcharges on logistics warehousing business entities. In such cases, "Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport" shall be construed as "Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport or the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries", "Article 18(1) of the Act" as "Article 21-9(1) of the Act", and "Article 18(3) of the Act" as "Article 21-9(3) of the Act", respectively.
  [This Article Added on Jul. 19, 2022]

CHAPTER IV DEVELOPMENT AND OPERATION OF LOGISTICS COMPLEXES

Article 13 (Designation of general logistics complexes) (1) Deleted. <Oct. 8, 2020>
  (2) Where he or she intends to modify any important matters prescribed by Presidential Decree in the latter part of Article 22(2) of the Act and the latter part of paragraph (3) of that Article means where he or she intends to modify any of the following matters. <Amended on Jun. 28, 2016>
  1. Alteration of the area designated as a general logistics complex (limited to cases where at least 1/10 of the area is altered);
  2. Alteration of the area of a site for facilities of a general logistics complex (limited to cases where not less than 1/10 of the area is altered) or alteration of the use of a site for facilities of a general logistics complex;
  3. Alteration of the area of a site for infrastructure (including ditches) or alteration of the location of such infrastructure (limited to an alteration of at least 1/10 of the area);
  4. Modification of the implementer of the general logistics complex development project.
  [Title Amended on Jun. 28, 2016]

Article 14 (Request for designation of general logistics complexes) (1) When the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport or a Mayor/Do Governor designates a general logistics complex pursuant to Article 22(2) or (3) of the Act, he or she shall designate a general logistics complex only where it meets the general logistics complex development plan and the guidelines for development of logistics complexes under Article 15. <Amended on Jun. 28, 2016>
  (2) A person who intends to request the designation of a general logistics complex pursuant to Article 22(4) of the Act shall submit a draft general logistics complex development plan to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport or the competent Mayor/Do Governor, along with the following documents and drawings: <Amended on Jun. 28, 2016>
  1. Location map, facility layout map, and bird's-eye view;
  2. Documents concerning the current status of land utilization in an area subject to designation;
  3. Documents concerning the analysis of location conditions, such as water, energy, traffic, and communications facilities;
  4. Documents concerning a disposal plan for the developed land, facilities, etc. (in the disposal plan, the location and area of the land, facilities, etc. to be supplied as a general logistics complex development project, the method of determining the price thereof, the qualification requirements for persons to be supplied with the land, facilities, etc., the method of selection, the timing and date of supply; methods and conditions, matters concerning lease management, etc. shall be included; hereinafter the same shall apply);
  5. Documents concerning relocation measures.
  (3) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport or the Mayor/Do Governor deems that an area requested to be designated as a general logistics complex under paragraph (2) is inappropriate for designation as a general logistics complex, he or she shall notify the person who has made such request of the grounds therefor. <Amended on Jun. 28, 2016>
  (4) "Other matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 22(5)9 of the Act means the following matters. <Amended on Jun. 28, 2016>
  1. A plan for supporting major facilities for the development of a general logistics complex;
  2. Where replotting is necessary, a replotting plan.
  [Title Amended on Jun. 28, 2016]

Article 14-2 (Designation of urban advanced logistics complexes) (1) Article 13(2) and 14(1) and (4) shall apply mutatis mutandis to procedures for designating urban advanced logistics complexes and development plans under Article 22-2(3) of the Act.
  (2) Facilities that the implementer of an urban advanced logistics complex development project shall provide to the State or a local government pursuant to Article 22-2(4) of the Act or operating expenses therefor shall be an amount calculated according to the standards determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport within the limit of 25/100 of the land value of the relevant site.
  (3) The value of land for the site subject to development under paragraph (2) shall be calculated based on the date the approval of the implementation plan for the development of a logistics complex is publicly notified pursuant to Article 29(1) of the Act, and the amount calculated by arithmetically averaging the amounts appraised by at least two appraisal corporations, etc. under the Act on Appraisal and Certified Appraisers shall be the amount. <Amended on Aug. 31, 2016; Jan. 21, 2022>
  (4) "Public interest facilities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 22-2(4)4 of the Act means the following facilities:
  1. Public facilities defined in subparagraph 13 of Article 2 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act;
  2. Public, cultural and athletic facilities under Article 2(1)4 of the Enforcement Decree of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act;
  3. General medical facilities among health and sanitary facilities under Article 2(1)6 of the Enforcement Decree of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act;
  4. Waste treatment facilities among environmental infrastructure under Article 2(1)7 of the Enforcement Decree of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act;
  5. Public housing under subparagraph 1a or b of Article 2 of the Special Act on Public Housing.
  [This Article Added on Jun. 28, 2016]

Article 14-3 (Consent of land owners) (1) The methods of calculating the number of consenters under Article 22-3(2) of the Act shall be as follows:
  1. Where one parcel of land is jointly owned by several persons: Only one representative co-owner who has obtained consent from other co-owners shall be deemed the owner of the relevant land; provided, the sectional owners defined in subparagraph 2 of Article 2 of the Act on Ownership and Management of Condominium Buildings shall be deemed one landowner.
  2. Where one building is jointly owned by several persons: Only one representative co-owner who has obtained consent from other co-owners shall be deemed the owner of the relevant building.
  3. Where the number of landowners and building owners increases due to the division of sectional ownership under subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Act on Ownership and Management of Condominium Buildings after the date of public announcement under Article 17(1): The number of landowners and building owners shall be calculated based on the number of owners before the date of public announcement, and the increased number of owners shall not be additionally included in the total number of owners.
  4. A person who has no resident registration number as at the time he or she is registered as an owner in a certified copy of the land register, a certified copy of the building register, a certified copy of the land register, a certified copy of the building register, a certified copy of the land register and a certified copy of the building register and a certified copy of the building register, and whose whereabouts are unknown, where his or her address is currently different from the current address, shall be excluded from the number of landowners, superficies, and building owners.
  (2) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport or a Mayor/Do Governor intends to obtain consent or withdrawal of consent from a landowner, superficies holder, or building owner, he or she shall obtain a written consent or a written withdrawal of consent prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, and shall obtain a written consent or a written withdrawal of consent from the representative owners of public land, superficies, or buildings, and shall receive additional written consent from the representative owners of public land, superficies, or buildings.
  (3) Except as otherwise provided for in paragraphs (1) and (2), detailed matters concerning the methods, procedures, etc. for calculating the number of consenters shall be prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.
  [This Article Added on Jun. 28, 2016]

Article 14-4 (Special cases concerning supply of housing to employees of tenant enterprises) (1) A person who constructs and supplies housing in a support complex under Article 22-4(1) of the Act may specially supply housing within 50/100 of the construction quantity (30/100 in cases of an urban high-tech logistics complex located in an overconcentration control region under Article 6(1)1 of the Seoul Metropolitan Area Readjustment Planning Act) to employees, etc. of prospective enterprises or of educational or research institutes pursuant to paragraph (3) of that Article.
  (2) The eligibility for tenancy and the method for selecting tenants of housing specially supplied pursuant to paragraph (1) shall be prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.
  [This Article Added on Jun. 28, 2016]

Article 14-5 (Multi-dimensional development with other zones) "District prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as a public housing zone defined in subparagraph 2 of Article 2 of the Special Act on Public Housing" in Article 22-5 of the Act means a public housing zone defined in subparagraph 2 of Article 2 of the Special Act on Public Housing.
  [This Article Added on Jun. 28, 2016]

Article 15 (Details of guidelines for development of logistics complexes) (1) Guidelines for development of logistics complexes under Article 22-6(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "Guidelines for Development of Logistics Complexes") shall include the following matters: <Amended on Jul. 20, 2012; Jun. 28, 2016; May 7, 2024>
  1. Matters concerning planned and systematic Development of logistics complexes;
  2. Matters concerning the designation, development, and support of logistics complexes;
  3. Matters concerning environmental conservation, such as strategic environmental impact assessment, small-scale environmental impact assessment, and environmental impact assessment under the Environmental Impact Assessment Act;
  4. Matters to be considered for balanced development between regions;
  5. Matters to be considered for the preservation of national heritage;
  6. Matters necessary for the stabilization of land prices;
  7. Matters concerning the determination of sale prices;
  8. Matters concerning the supply of land, facilities, etc.
  (2) Logistics complex development guidelines shall be formulated so that sites for facilities of logistics complexes are appropriately allocated for the balanced development between regions.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Aug. 11, 2010]

Article 16 (Public notice of designation or alteration of logistics complexes) (1) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 23(1) of the Act means the following: <Amended on Oct. 14, 2010; Feb. 2, 2012; Apr. 10, 2012; Jun. 28, 2016>
  1. The name, location, and size of the logistics complex;
  2. The objectives of designation of the logistics complex;
  3. The implementer of the logistics complex development project;
  4. The period and method of development of the logistics complex;
  5. A land utilization plan and a plan for major infrastructure;
  5-2. A building plan and a plan for the utilization of complex sites under the proviso of Article 22-2(3) of the Act (limited to where an urban advanced logistics complex is designated or the details of such designation are modified);
  6. Major types of business to be invited and a plan for the placement of types of business to be invited [including a placement plan for the relevant enterprise, where a person who designates a logistics complex pursuant to Article 22(1) or 22-2(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "person authorized to designate logistics complexes") and an enterprise wishing to move into a logistics complex concludes a tenancy agreement];
  7. Where land, buildings, structures or fixtures on the land subject to expropriation or use, rights other than ownership thereof, mining rights, fishery rights, and rights to use water (hereinafter referred to as "land, etc.") exist, the details thereof and the names and addresses of the relevant persons defined in subparagraph 5 of Article 2 of the Act on Acquisition of and Compensation for Land, etc. for Public Works Projects and the owners thereof;
  8. A plan for supporting major facilities for the development of a logistics complex;
  9. Land substitution plan for former landowners;
  10. A master plan for reclamation of public waters under Articles 22 and 27 of the Public Waters Management and Reclamation Act;
  11. An Urban/Gun management plan under Article 30 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act;
  12. Topographical drawings, etc. under Article 8(3) of the Framework Act on the Regulation of Land Use;
  13. Methods of perusal of related books.
  (2) Where the matters referred to in paragraph (1)3, 7, or 9 are not finalized when designating a logistics complex, such matters may be separately publicly notified after the details thereof are finalized.
  (3) When a Mayor/Do Governor publicly notifies the matters referred to in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1) after designating a logistics complex or altering the designation thereof, he or she shall notify the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport of the details of such public notice without delay. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Mar. 23, 2013>

Article 17 (Hearing of opinions from residents) (1) Where an authority designating logistics complexes intends to hear opinions of residents and relevant experts on the designation of a logistics complex pursuant to Article 24(1) of the Act, he or she shall send the details of a draft logistics complex development plan to the Special Self-Governing City Mayor, the Special Self-Governing Province Governor, or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu (referring to the head of an autonomous Gu; hereinafter referred to as the "head of a Si/Gun/Gu") having jurisdiction over the location of the relevant logistics complex, and the head of a Si/Gun/Gu in receipt of such draft logistics complex development plan shall publicly announce the main contents thereof through daily newspapers, official newsletters, website, broadcasting, etc. published in the relevant local area and make them available to the general public for inspection for at least 14 days. <Amended on Nov. 24, 2020>
  (2) A person who has an opinion on the details of a draft logistics complex development plan publicly announced pursuant to paragraph (1) may submit a written opinion to the head of the relevant Si/Gun/Gu within the perusal period.
  (3) The head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall submit to the authority designating logistics complexes a review opinion on the opinions submitted pursuant to paragraph (2) to the person authorized to designate logistics complexes.
  (4) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 24(1) of the Act means the following:
  1. Alteration of the area designated as a logistics complex (limited to cases where at least 1/10 of the area is altered);
  2. Alteration of the area of a site for facilities of a logistics complex (limited to cases where less than 1/10 of the area is altered) or alteration of the use of a site for facilities of a logistics complex;
  3. Alteration of the area of a site for infrastructure (including ditches) or alteration of the location of such infrastructure (limited to an alteration of less than 1/10 of the area).
  (5) Where the authority designating logistics complexes intends to omit the hearing of opinions of residents and relevant experts pursuant to the proviso to Article 24(1) of the Act, he or she shall consult with the heads of relevant administrative agencies in advance.

Article 18 (Objects of permission for acts) (1) Activities subject to permission from the head of a Si/Gun/Gu pursuant to Article 25(1) of the Act shall be as follows: <Amended on Jan. 5, 2021>
  1. Construction of buildings: Construction, substantial repair, or change of the use of buildings, etc., (including temporary buildings) defined in Article 2(1)2 of the Building Act;
  ACT ON THE DEVELOPMENT AND MANAGEMENT OF LOGISTICS FACILITIES
  3. Change in the form and quality of land: Change in the shape of land by such means as cutting of land, filling-up of earth, leveling of land, or paving with earth, excavation of land, or reclamation of public waters;
  4. Gathering of soil and stone: Gathering of soil and stone, such as earth, sand, gravel, and rocks; provided, subparagraph 3 shall apply to the gathering with the purpose of changing the form and quality of land);
  5. Division of land;
  6. Piling up goods: Piling up goods which are not easy to move for at least one month;
  7. Felling and planting bamboo and trees.
  (2) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu intends to grant permission for any act referred to in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1) pursuant to Article 25(1) of the Act, if the implementer of a logistics complex development project (hereinafter referred to as "implementer") is designated pursuant to Article 27 of the Act, he or she shall hear opinions of the implementer in advance.
  (3) Other activities prescribed by Presidential Decree in Article 25(2)2 of the Act means any of the following activities which are not subject to permission for development activities under Article 56 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act: <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Mar. 23, 2013>
  1. Installation of simple structures prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, which are directly used for the production of agricultural, forestry, and fishery products;
  2. Alteration of the form and quality of land for cultivation;
  3. Extracting soil and rocks within the extent not hindering the development of a logistics complex and damaging natural scenery;
  4. Piling goods in a site determined to be retained in a logistics complex;
  5. Temporary planting of ornamental bamboo and trees (excluding temporary planting in arable land).
  (4) A person required to file a report pursuant to Article 25(3) of the Act shall file a report with the head of the competent Si/Gun/Gu along with the progress of the relevant construction works or project and an implementation plan within 30 days from the date the logistics complex is designated and publicly notified.

Article 19 (Cancellation of designation of logistics complexes) (1) Period prescribed by Presidential Decree in Article 26(1) of the Act means five years.
  (2) Where the authority designating logistics complexes intends to cancel the designation of a logistics complex pursuant to Article 26(2) of the Act, he or she shall consult with the heads of relevant administrative agencies, specifying the following matters:
  1. Grounds for and details of cancellation;
  2. Matters concerning the reinstatement of a special-purpose area under Article 36 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act.
  (3) Where the designation of a logistics complex is revoked pursuant to Article 26(1) and (2) of the Act, the authority designating logistics complexes shall publicly notify the following matters:
  1. The name of the logistics complex;
  2. The location and size of the logistics complex to be canceled;
  3. Grounds for canceling the designation of a logistics complex;
  4. Matters concerning the reinstatement of a special-purpose area under Article 36 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act;
  5. Methods of perusal of related books.

Article 20 (Implementers) (1) When designating an implementer pursuant to Article 27(1) of the Act, an authority designating logistics complexes shall take into account the feasibility of a project plan, the ability to raise funds, the relationship with a development plan formulated pursuant to other Acts, etc. when designating an implementer.
  (2) "Public institutions prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 27(2)2 of the Act means the following Acts: <Amended on Jun. 26, 2009; Sep. 21, 2009>
  1. The Korea Land and Housing Corporation incorporated under the Korea Land and Housing Corporation Act;
  2. The Korea Expressway Corporation under the Korea Expressway Corporation Act;
  3. Deleted; <Sep. 21, 2009>
  4. The Korea Water Resources Corporation under the Korea Water Resources Corporation Act;
  5. The Korea Rural Community Corporation under the Korea Rural Community Corporation and Farmland Management Fund Act;
  6. The Port Authority under the Port Authority Act.
  (3) A person who intends to be designated as an implementer pursuant to Article 27(3) of the Act shall submit an application for designation as an implementer, stating the following matters, to the authority designating logistics complexes:
  1. The name and address of the person who intends to implement the project (in cases of a corporation, its name and the name of its representative, if the person is a corporation);
  2. The name and location of the logistics complex where the project is to be implemented and the area of the project to be implemented;
  3. Outline of the project plan, such as the name, purpose, outline, implementation period, and implementation method of the project.
  (4) Application for designation of an implementer under paragraph (3) shall be accompanied by the following documents and drawings:
  1. A location map;
  2. A business plan;
  3. A financing plan.

Article 21 (Vicarious execution of development projects) (1) An implementer may, if deemed necessary for developing a site for logistics complex facilities concurrently with constructing logistics complex facilities or for efficiently implementing a logistics complex development project, assign a tenant enterprise or a support institution pursuant to Article 27(5) of the Act to execute the site development from among the logistics complex development projects for facilities for the relevant tenant enterprises or support institutions.
  (2) Where an implementer intends to have any tenant enterprise or support institution to vicariously execute a part of a logistics complex development project pursuant to Article 27(5) of the Act, he or she shall enter into a contract thereon. In such cases, the implementer shall submit a report on the vicarious execution of the logistics complex development project to the relevant authority designating logistics complexes, along with a copy of the contract, within 14 days from the date the contract is concluded.
  (3) Any project implementer shall guide and supervise an agent for a logistics complex development project who has entered into a contract under paragraph (2) so that the agent can faithfully implement the project in accordance with the contract.

Article 22 (Approval of implementation plans) (1) Where an implementer intends to apply for approval of an implementation plan for the development of a logistics complex under Article 28(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "implementation plan"), he or she shall submit an application for approval of an implementation plan stating the following matters to the authority designating logistics complexes:
  1. The name and address of the implementer (in cases of a corporation, its name and the name of its representative);
  2. The name of a project;
  3. The purpose of a project;
  4. The location and area of the project to be implemented;
  5. Methods and period for implementing the project;
  6. Current status of land utilization in the area where the project is to be implemented;
  7. A land utilization plan and a plan for infrastructure;
  8. A plan for the devolvement and management of public facilities.
  (2) The following documents and drawings shall be attached to the application for approval of an implementation plan under paragraph (1): <Amended on Dec. 31, 2009; Feb. 8, 2010; Oct. 14, 2010; Apr. 10, 2012; Jan. 22, 2016; May 7, 2024; Dec. 31, 2024>
  1. A location map;
  2. A land map prepared according to the cadastral map;
  3. A proposed ground plan and drawings and specifications of working design (if reclamation of public waters is included, it includes a description of reclamation work that must be submitted pursuant to Article 48(1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Public Waters Management and Reclamation Act);
  4. Project cost and financing plan (including annual investment plan);
  5. Documents on disposition of developed land or Facilities;
  6. A detailed statement of existing logistics complex facilities, buildings, etc. to be retained in the project area;
  7. Documents concerning the purchase of land, buildings, rights, etc. in the project area, compensation therefor, and measures for relocation of residents;
  8. Details of land, etc., if any, and the owner thereof, and the name and address of a relevant person defined in subparagraph 5 Article 2 of the Act on Acquisition of and Compensation for Land, etc. for Public Works Projects;
  9. A plan for the gratuitous reversion, etc. of public facilities, land, etc.;
  10. Relevant documents and drawings necessary for the determination on urban or Gun management planning;
  11. A marine use consultation form to be submitted pursuant to Article 11(1) of the Marine Use Impact Assessment Act (attached only in cases of reclamation of public waters);
  12. In cases of a project subject to environmental impact assessment under the Environmental Impact Assessment Act or a project subject to traffic impact assessment under the Urban Traffic Improvement Promotion Act, an environmental impact assessment report or a traffic impact assessment report;
  13. Documents on measures for the preservation of national heritage.
  (3) "An important matter prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the latter part of Article 28(1) of the Act means the following: <Amended on Dec. 14, 2019; Jun. 1, 2015>
  1. Change of the address of the implementer;
  2. Change of the representative of an implementer who is a corporation;
  3. Correction of the implementation area due to errors, etc. within the scope of not changing the project implementation area;
  4. Change of the area where the project is implemented by dividing it within the scope not exceeding the project implementation area;
  5. Reduction of the area within the scope of 10/100 of the area where the project is implemented;
  6. Increase or decrease in the project cost within the limit of 10/100 of the project cost;
  7. Change of the site area varying on the result of a cadastral confirmation survey pursuant to subparagraph 2 of Article 45 of the Act on the Establishment and Management of Spatial Data.

Article 23 (Public notice of approval for implementation plans) Matters subject to public notice under Article 29(1) of the Act shall be as follows: <Amended on Apr. 10, 2012; Jan 26, 2021>
  1. The name of a project;
  2. The name of the implementer (in cases of a corporation, its name and the name of its representative);
  3. The purpose and outline of the projects;
  4. The location and area of the implementation area;
  5. Project implementation period (including scheduled date of starting and completion);
  6. Matters referred to in the subparagraphs of Article 25(6) of the Enforcement Decree of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act concerning urban/Gun planning facilities.

Article 24 (Entrusted implementation of logistics complex development projects) (1) "Other public facilities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 31(1) of the Act means roads, waterworks, railroads, utility tunnels, public wastewater treatment facilities, waste treatment facilities, integrated energy supply facilities, embankments, revetments (shores and bank protective facilities), tide embankment. protection facilities), tide embankments, estuary barrage, and greenbelt facilities. <Amended on Jan. 17, 2017; Jun. 5, 2018; Jan. 5, 2021>
  (2) Where an implementer intends to entrust part of a logistics complex development project to the State, a local government, or a public institution pursuant to Article 31(1) of the Act, he or she shall consult with a person to be entrusted with such project on the following matters:
  1. Business site of the entrusted project;
  2. The type, scale, and amount of the entrusted project, and other matters that serve as the standards for construction design;
  3. Implementation period of an entrusted project (including scheduled date of starting and completion);
  4. Matters concerning the method of paying expenses necessary for the entrusted project and the management of such funds;
  5. Where a truster provides real estate, equipment, materials, or workers, matters concerning the management thereof;
  6. Matters concerning risk bearing;
  7. Other matters necessary for clarifying the details of the entrusted project.
  (3) "A public institution prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 31(1) of the Act means the following institutions in the subparagraphs of Article 20(2).
  (4) Where an implementer referred to in Article 27(2)4 through 6 of the Act intends to obtain approval of a trust contract pursuant to Article 31(3) of the Act, he or she shall submit an application for approval of a trust contract to the authority designating logistics complexes, along with the following documents: <Added on Dec. 9, 2022>
  1. The name and address of the truster and the trustee (in cases of a corporation, referring to the name and address of the corporation and the name and address of its representative);
  2. The name, location, and area of the logistics complex;
  3. Outline of the trust development project including the purpose, type, and trust period of the trust development;
  4. A logistics complex development project plan, including the following matters:
  a. A location map of the logistics complex development project;
  b. A financing plan for the logistics complex development project;
  c. A plan for disposal of land, facilities, etc. created by a logistics complex development project.
  (5) Where an implementer referred to in Article 27(2)4 through 6 of the Act concludes a trust contract with approval under paragraph (4), he or she shall submit a copy of the contract to the authority designating logistics complexes within one month from the date of concluding the contract. <Added on Dec. 9, 2022>
  [Title Amended on Dec. 9, 2022]

Article 25 (Land substitution to land owners) (1) "Support facilities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 34(1) of the Act means the facilities classified as follows: <Amended on Feb. 6, 2024>
  1. In the case of a logistics complex developed by an implementer referred to in Article 27(2)1 through 5 of the Act: Facilities referred to in subparagraph 8a through c of Article 2 of the Act;
  2. In the case of a logistics complex developed by an implementer under Article 27(2)6 of the Act: Facilities referred to in the items of subparagraph 8 of Article 2 of the Act.
  (2) A land owner eligible for land substitution pursuant to Article 34(1) of the Act shall be a person who owns land in the logistics complex that is larger than the minimum supply area specified in the logistics complex development plan as of the date of designation and announcement of the logistics complex, and who intend to install the following facilities on the relevant land. <Amended on Feb. 6, 2024>
  1. In the case of a logistics complex developed by an implementer referred to in Article 27(2)1 through 5 of the Act: Logistics complex facilities suitable for the types of business to be invited specified in the logistics complex development plan or facilities referred to in paragraph (1)1;
  2. In the case of a logistics complex developed by an implementer referred to in Article 27(2)6 of the Act: Logistics complex facilities suitable for the types of business to be invited specified in the logistics complex development plan or facilities referred to in paragraph (1)2.
  (3) A person who intends to obtain land substitution pursuant to Article 34(1) of the Act shall submit to a project implementer an application for land substitution to an implementer, along with a plan for installation of facilities. <Amended on Feb. 6, 2024>
  (4) An application for land substitution under paragraph (3) shall be filed by an implementer during the consultation period specified in the public announcement of compensation for the relevant logistics complex. <Amended on Feb. 6, 2024>
  (5) An implementer (excluding an implementer referred to in Article 27(2)6 of the Act) shall determine the methods, procedures, etc. for land substitution in the logistics complex development plan in accordance with the following standards: <Amended on Feb. 6, 2024>
  1. The value of the previous land subject to land substitution shall be the amount of compensation for consultation presented by the implementer at the time of public announcement of compensation, and the value of the land substitution shall be based on the sale price for each site of the relevant logistics complex under Article 39;
  2. The large area of land substitution shall be based on the previous area of land, but the area may be increased or decreased in consideration of regional conditions, supply and demand conditions, etc., of logistics complexes;
  3. The difference between the values of the previous land and of the substituted land shall be paid in cash.

Article 26 (Scope of public facilities) Public Facilities under Article 36 of the Act means the following facilities among public facilities under subparagraph 13 of Article 2 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act:
  1. Roads;
  2. Parks;
  3. Squares;
  4. Parking lots (limited to those established by the State or a local government);
  5. Railroads;
  6. Rivers;
  7. Greenbelts;
  8. Playgrounds (limited to playgrounds established by the State or a local government);
  9. Public vacant land;
  10. Waterworks (limited to pipelines in cases of waterworks installed by the Korea Water Resources Corporation);
  11. Sewage;
  12. Utility tunnels;
  13. Reservoir facilities;
  14. Ditches.

Article 27 (Scope and timing of installation of electric facilities) (1) The scope of installation of electric power system, telecommunications system, facilities for supply of gas, and regional heating system under Article 38(2) of the Act shall be as follows. <Amended on Apr. 10, 2012; Jan. 5, 2021>
  1. Electric power system: Electric power system facilities from key facilities outside the logistics complex to the boundary line of a lot of land (hereinafter referred to as an "individual lot") adjoining an urban or Gun planning road of at least six meters in the land use plan within the logistics complex;
  2. Telecommunications system: Pipeline facilities from key facilities outside the logistics complex to the boundary lines of an individual lot in the logistics complex, and key cable facilities outside the logistics complex to the first terminal of an individual lot in the logistics complex;
  3. Facilities for supply of gas: Facilities for supply of gas from key gas supply facilities outside the logistics complex to the boundary lines of individual lots within the logistics complex; provided, where a static pressure control room (for purposes of pressure maintenance and control) is installed in a lot of land in the logistics complex to supply gas for cooking or unit heating (excluding centralized heating), gas supply facilities to the static pressure control room:
  4. Regional heating system: Heating pipelines running from the point of divergence of key heating pipelines outside the logistics complex to a closing valve at the entrance to each engine room in an individual lot within the logistics complex.
  (2) When the authority designating logistics complexes has approved an implementation plan, he or she shall, without delay, notify the installer of electric power system, telecommunications system, gas supply facilities, or regional heating facilities under Article 38(2) of the Act of such fact.
  (3) The installation of facilities under paragraph (1) shall be completed by the date of filing an application for approval for completion under Article 46 of the Act (where the authority designating logistics complexes is an implementer, the date of completion of the logistics complex development project), unless there is a compelling reason not to do so.

Article 28 (Subsidization or loan of expenses) The items of expenses that the State or a local government may provide subsidies or loans under Article 39(1) of the Act shall be as follows: <Amended on Jan. 17, 2017; May 7, 2024; Mar. 25, 2025>
  1. Construction cost of arterial roads of a logistics complex;
  2. Expenses incurred in constructing greenbelts in the logistics complex;
  3. Expenses for projects for relocation measures;
  4. Costs for the development and purchase of sites for facilities of the logistics complex and sites for supporting facilities;
  5. Construction costs of water supply facilities, sewage, and public wastewater treatment facilities;
  6. Expenses for investigations into national heritage.
  7. Other costs prescribed by ordinance of the relevant local government with respect to a logistics complex development project, in cases where a local government provides a subsidy or a loan.

Article 29 (Support for installation of infrastructure) Infrastructure supported by the State or a local government pursuant to Article 39(2) of the Act shall be as follows: <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Mar. 23, 2013>
  1. Roads, railroads, and harbor facilities;
  2. Water supply facilities and communications facilities;
  3. Sewage facilities and waste disposal facilities;
  4. Utility tunnels in a logistics complex;
  5. Integrated energy supply facilities;
  6. Other public facilities prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, which are particularly necessary for the development of a logistics complex.

Article 30 (Financial resources of special accounts for development of logistics complexes) "Ratio prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 40(2)6 of the Act means 10 percent; provided, in cases prescribed otherwise by ordinance of the relevant local government, it shall refer to the ratio thereof. <Amended on Nov. 16, 2023>

Article 31 (Purpose of special accounts for development of logistics complexes) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 41(1)7 of the Act means the following:
  1. Project costs of logistics complex development projects implemented by local governments;
  2. Matters prescribed by municipal ordinance of the relevant local government.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Nov. 16, 2023]

Article 32 (Operation and management of special accounts for development of logistics complexes) (1) Where the scope of matters that may be subsidized from the special account for development of a logistics complex by ordinance of the relevant local government pursuant to Article 41(3) of the Act is prescribed, the scope thereof shall be as follows. <Amended on Apr. 10, 2012; Nov. 1, 2022>
  1. The following project costs implemented by the head of the relevant local government:
  a. Costs of construction of the logistics complex development project;
  b. Construction costs of urban/Gun planning facility projects and compensation costs for private sites under subparagraph 10 of Article 2 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act related to logistics complex development projects.
  2. Not more than 1/2 of the following costs of projects to be implemented by a person other than those referred to in subparagraph 1:
  a. Construction costs necessary for the installation of urban/Gun planning facilities among logistics complex development projects;
  b. Construction costs of urban/Gun planning facility projects under subparagraph 10 of Article 2 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act related to logistics complex development projects.
  3. Expenses incurred in conducting surveys and research under Article 41(1)4 of the Act;
  4. Expenses under Article 41(1)6 of the Act.
  (2) Where the scope of matters that may be loaned from the special account for development of a logistics complex by ordinance of the relevant local government pursuant to Article 41(3) of the Act is prescribed, the scope thereof shall be as follows: <Amended on Apr. 10, 2012; Nov. 1, 2022>
  1.Not more than 1/2 of the construction cost of an urban/Gun planning facility project defined in subparagraph 10 of article 2 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act implemented by the head of the relevant local government related to the logistics complex development project;
  2. Not more than 1/3 of the following costs of projects to be implemented by a person other than those referred to in subparagraph 1:
  a. Construction costs necessary for the installation of urban/Gun planning facilities among logistics complex development projects;
  b. Construction costs of urban/Gun planning facility projects under subparagraph 10 of Article 2 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act related to logistics complex development projects.

Article 33 (Advance payments) (1) An implementer who intends to receive an advance payment under Article 43 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "advance payment") shall meet the following requirements: <Amended on Feb. 2, 2012>
  1. An implementer falling under Article 27(2)1 through 3 of the Act: He or she shall obtain approval for an implementation plan;
  2. An implementer falling under Article 27(2)4 and 5 of the Act: he or she shall meet all of the following requirements:
  a. He or she shall obtain approval of an implementation plan;
  b. He or she shall have secured the ownership of the land to be parceled out and cancel the mortgage established on the relevant land; provided, where it fails to secure the ownership of land or to cancel the mortgage due to unavoidable reasons, the implementer, landowner and mortgagee shall notarize a joint agreement with the following details and submit it to the person authorized to approve implementation plans under Article 28(1) of the Act:
  1) No landowner shall transfer the relevant land to a third party or offer it as security;
  2) Where a person who has paid the relevant price pursuant to Article 43 of the Act uses the relevant land after obtaining approval for completion or permission for use before approval for completion, the landowner and the mortgagee shall transfer ownership without delay and cancel the mortgage;
  c. The progress ratio of construction works for the development project for the land to be sold shall have reached at least 10/100;
  d. A letter of guarantee, etc. (a letter of guarantee, insurance policy, term deposit, beneficiary certificates, etc., referred to in the subparagraphs of Article 37(2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Act on Contracts to Which the State Is a Party, in order to guarantee the refund of an advance payment in cases of non-performance of a contract for sale in units shall be submitted to the authority designating logistics complexes:
  1) The amount of guarantee or insurance shall be at least the amount obtained by adding the amount equivalent to the agreed interest corresponding to the guarantee or insurance period (referring to the amount calculated according to the level of interest rates on loan on bills of commercial banks, excluding local banks) to the advance payment;
  2) The commencement date of the guarantee or insurance period shall be before the date an advance payment is received, and the end date shall be at least 30 days after the completion date; provided, where the business period is extended, a letter of guarantee, etc. stating that the period of guarantee or insurance is the period of adding the extended period to the original period of guarantee or insurance shall be submitted.
  (2) After receiving an advance payment under paragraph (1), no implementer shall provide a site or facility he or she has created as security.
  (3) Where an implementer fails to perform a project according to the terms and conditions of a sales contract or is deemed incapable of performing the project, the authority designating logistics complexes may use a letter of guarantee, etc. for the refund of advance payment before the completion of the relevant logistics complex.

Article 34 (Construction of public facilities) (1) Public facilities prescribed by Presidential Decree in Article 44 of the Act means the following facilities: <Amended on Apr. 10, 2012; Apr. 7, 2026>
  1. Access roads to logistics complexes and arterial roads;
  2. Parks and green areas in logistics complexes (referring to parks and green areas determined as urban or Gun Planning Facilities)
  3. Water supply facilities, sewage facilities, telecommunications facilities, and waste disposal facilities;
  4. Public facilities gratuitously reverted to the state or local governments pursuant to Article 36 of the Act.
  (2) Expenses incurred in installing public facilities under paragraph (1) shall be the sum of land costs, land charges, development expenses, infrastructure installation expenses, direct labor costs, relocation measures expenses, sales expenses, general management expenses, capital expenses, and other expenses calculated in accordance with the standards under Article 39(3).
  (3) In applying Article 44 of the Act, where at least 2 project operators exist, expenses incurred in installing public facilities in the relevant logistics complex shall be borne by each project operator separately according to the ratio of the total available area (including the total site area for existing facilities, etc.) of the relevant logistics complex to be sold by the project operator to the total available area (including the total site area for existing facilities, etc.) of the relevant logistics complex. <Amended on Apr. 7, 2026>
  (4) Notwithstanding paragraph (3), where public facilities are installed only for the purpose of use by a certain implementer, the relevant implementer who is to use the public facilities may be required to fully or partially bear expenses incurred in installing the public facilities, taking into comprehensive consideration the location of the public facilities, the purpose of installation, the current status of use, local conditions, etc.
  (5) Deleted. <Apr. 7, 2026>
  (6) Deleted. <Apr. 7, 2026>
  [Title Amended on Apr. 7, 2026]

Article 34-2 Deleted. <Apr. 7, 2026>

Article 35 (Employment of resettled residents) (1) Where deemed necessary to stabilize the livelihood of resettled residents or residents in neighboring areas pursuant to Article 45(2) of the Act, an implementer may prepare a job-seeking table of job seekers and a job-offering tableof tenant enterprises, and file an application for job seeking or job offer with the head of the competent employment security office or the head of the competent Si/Gun/Gu.
  (2) The head of the competent employment security office or the head of the competent Si/Gun/Gu who has received an application for job-seeking or job-offering pursuant to paragraph (1) shall present a list of job-seekers who meet the conditions for job-offering to the job offerers, and shall actively arrange employment for the job-seekers by presenting a list of job-offerers who meet the conditions for job-seeking to the job-seekers.

Article 36 (Approval for completion) (1) Where an implementer intends to obtain approval for completion pursuant to Article 46(1) of the Act, he or she shall submit an application for approval for completion, stating the following matters, to the authority designating logistics complexes:
  1. The name and address of the implementer (in cases of a corporation, its name and the name of its representative);
  2. The name of a project;
  3. The location and area of the implementation area;
  4. Project implementation period;
  5. A land use plan;
  6. Infrastructure plan.
  (2) Application for approval for completion under paragraph (1) shall be accompanied by the following documents and drawings: <Amended on Oct. 14, 2010; Aug. 31, 2016; Jan. 21, 2022>
  1. As-built drawings and specifications (including as-built photographs);
  2. Cadastral survey results charts issued by the head of a Si/Gun/Gu;
  3. Jurisdiction records and drawings of public facilities, land, etc. prescribed in Article 36 of the Act (including appraisal records for public facilities, land, etc., whose purposes are abolished, by an appraisal corporation, etc. prescribed in the Act on Appraisal and Certified Appraisers and construction cost calculation sheets of public facilities newly installed, where a project implementer is one under Article 27(2)5 of the Act);
  4. A land substitution plan and a comparison map of the old and new land cadastre (to be attached only where land substitution is made pursuant to Article 34 of the Act);
  5. Itemized statements of land to be obtained by an implementer and of land, etc. to be reverted to the State or a local government under Article 46 and Article 35(4) of the Public Waters Management And Reclamation Act and Article 51 of the Enforcement Decree of that Act (appended only where public waters are reclaimed);
  6. Drawings of land, facilities, etc. before and after completion;
  7. Comparison table of land and facilities before and after completion;
  8. Other documents stating matters necessary for the completion inspection.
  (3) Upon receipt of an application for approval for completion under paragraph (1), the authority designating logistics complexes shall conduct a completion inspection and issue a certificate of approval for completion, if the relevant logistics complex development project is deemed completed in compliance with the implementation plan approved pursuant to Article 28 of the Act.
  (4) "A public agency, research institute, and other specialized institution prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 46(2) of the Act means the following institutions: <Amended on Jun. 26, 2009; Sep. 21, 2009>
  1. The Korea Land and Housing Corporation incorporated under the Korea Land and Housing Corporation Act;
  2. The Korea Expressway Corporation under the Korea Expressway Corporation Act;
  3. The Korea Rural Community Corporation under the Korea Rural Community Corporation and Farmland Management Fund Act;
  4. The Korea Institute for Industrial Economics and Trade, the Korea Maritime Institute, the Korea Transport Institute, the Korea Rural Economic Institute, the Korea Rural Economic Institute, and the Korea Research Institute for Human Settlements under the Act on the Establishment, Operation and Fostering of Government-Funded Science and Technology Research Institutes and the Korea Institute of Civil Engineering and Building Technology under the Act on the Establishment, Operation and Fostering of Government-Funded Science and Technology Research Institutes;
  5. The Korea Water Resources Corporation under the Korea Water Resources Corporation Act;
  6. Deleted; <Sep. 21, 2009>
  7. The Port Authority under the Port Authority Act.
  (5) Matters to be publicly announced pursuant to Article 46(3) of the Act shall be as follows:
  1. The name of a project;
  2. The name and address of the implementer (in cases of a corporation, its name and the name of its representative);
  3. The location and area of the implementation area;
  4. Date of approval for completion;
  5. A plan for the management and disposal of public facilities, land, etc.;
  (6) Where an implementer obtains approval for completion pursuant to paragraph (3), he or she shall notify the management agency of the relevant logistics complex of the details referred to in the subparagraphs of paragraphs (1) and (2) within one month from the date of obtaining approval for completion.

Article 37 (Permission for use before approval for completion) (1) Where an implementer intends to use land developed or facilities installed pursuant to the proviso to Article 46(5) of the Act before authorization for completion, he or she shall determine the scope of use and submit an application for permission for use before authorization for completion to the authority designating logistics complexes, along with a written review on whether the implementation of the logistics complex development project is hindered, as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. If the land or facilities subject to an application for permission for use include State or public property in such cases, the implementer shall acquire in advance the ownership of the relevant property (excluding where the authority designating logistics complexes approves an implementation plan after hearing the opinions of the management authority on the gratuitous vesting and transfer of public facilities pursuant to Article 36(3) of the Act. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Mar. 23, 2013; May 8, 2018>
  (2) Upon receipt of an application for permission to use a logistics complex before approval for completion is granted under paragraph (1), the authority designating logistics complexes shall grant permission for use after closely checking whether the use of the logistics complex disrupts the logistics complex development project to be implemented in the future.
  (3) Upon receipt of an application from a person who intends to use the permitted land or facilities, an implementer who has obtained permission for use before authorization for completion pursuant to paragraph (2) shall allow the relevant land or facilities to be used without delay, except in extenuating circumstances.

Article 38 Deleted. <Aug. 11, 2010>

Article 39 (Determination of sale price) (1) Where an implementer sells land, facilities, etc. developed pursuant to Article 50(1) of the Act into facilities prescribed by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport as sites for logistics complex facilities or urban advanced logistics complex facilities, the sale price of such land, facilities, etc. shall be the sum of appropriate profits from the development cost; provided, where the implementer deems it necessary, the sale price may be an amount not exceeding such amount (in cases of public property, the amount under the Public Property and Commodity Management Act). <Amended on Jun. 28, 2016>
  (2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), an implementer may determine the sale price of land, facilities, etc. to be used for sale, such as a superstore, specialized shopping complex, etc. (excluding cases where land, facilities, etc. necessary for livelihood measures are supplied in lieu of land, facilities, etc. in consideration of the status of ownership of land, etc. originally owned by residents and their livelihood, etc.) by a competitive bidding conducted based on the appraised value under the Act on Appraisal and Certified Appraisers at the budget price. <Amended on Aug. 31, 2016; Jan. 5, 2021>
  (3) The development costs under paragraph (1) shall be the sum of land costs, land charges, development expenses, infrastructure installation expenses, direct labor costs, relocation measures expenses, sales expenses, general management expenses, capital expenses, and other expenses calculated in accordance with the standards under Appendix 2.
  (4) The appropriate profit referred to in paragraph (1) shall be determined by an implementer within the extent not exceeding 5/100 of the amount calculated under paragraph (3), excluding capital costs, expenses for vicarious execution of development projects under Article 27(5) of the Act, and advance payments, respectively, in consideration of demand for moving-in in the relevant logistics complex and regional circumstances, such as the promotion of balanced development among regions, etc.
  (5) Where an implementer sells a site for logistics complex facilities or facilities prescribed by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport as urban advanced logistics complex facilities under paragraph (1) before approval for completion has been granted, he or she may settle the sale price after authorization for completion based on the total project cost and appropriate profits invested in the relevant logistics complex development project. <Amended on Jun. 28, 2016>
  (6) Where an advance payment is made for a person who has paid an advance payment pursuant to paragraph (5), the amount equivalent to the interest rate on one-year term deposits of a commercial bank from the date of payment of the advance payment to the date of settlement shall be deducted from the adjusted amount.
  (7) The sale price of land, facilities, etc. supplied for purposes other than a site for logistics complex facilities or urban advanced logistics complex facilities prescribed in paragraph (1) shall be determined based on the appraised value under the Act on Appraisal and Certified Appraisers, and where an implementer deems it necessary, it may be determined by an amount not exceeding the amount under the Public Property and Commodity Management Act (in cases of public property, the amount under the Public Property and Commodity Management Act). <Amended on Jun. 28, 2016; Aug. 31, 2016>
  (8) Notwithstanding paragraph (7), where an implementer supplies land for the purpose of constructing privately constructed rental housing defined in subparagraph 2 of Article 2 of the Special Act on Private Rental Housing or publicly constructed rental housing defined in subparagraph 1-2 of Article 2 of the Special Act on Public Housing among facilities referred to in Article 2(4)2-2, the sale price of such land shall be the aggregate of appropriate profits from the development cost. In such cases, paragraphs (3) and (4) shall apply mutatis mutandis to the development cost and appropriate profits. <Added on Feb. 8, 2010; Dec. 28, 2015>

Article 40 (Standards for calculation of rent) Where an implementer leases land, facilities, etc. developed through a logistics complex development project pursuant to Article 50(1) of the Act, the standards for calculating the rent shall be as follows; provided, where the implementer deems it necessary, the rent may be determined by an amount not exceeding the amount: <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Aug. 11, 2010; Mar. 23, 2013; Aug. 31, 2016; Jan. 21, 2022>
  1. The first rent for land, facilities, etc. to be leased: The amount calculated by multiplying the sale price calculated pursuant to Article 39 by the rate of rent prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport;
  2. Rent where a contract is renewed due to the expiration, etc. of the rental period: the amount classified as follows:
  a. Where only land is leased, the amount obtained by multiplying the officially assessed individual land price calculated pursuant to Article 10 of the Act on the Public Announcement of Real Estate Values by the rate of rent prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport;
  b. Where land, facilities, etc. are leased together or only facilities, etc. are leased, the amount calculated by multiplying the appraised value appraised by an appraisal corporation, etc. under the Act on Appraisal and Certified Appraisers by the rate of rent prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport by the rate of rent prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.

Article 41 (Methods of supplying land, facilities) (1) An implementer shall sell or lease (hereinafter referred to as "supply") the land, facilities, etc. developed by the logistics complex development project according to the use specified in a logistics complex development plan formulated pursuant to Article 22(2) or (3) of the Act (including cases applied mutatis mutandis pursuant to Article 22-2(3) of the Act). In such cases, if deemed necessary for the smooth installation of infrastructure, the implementer may restrict the qualifications of persons to be supplied with the infrastructure or impose conditions on the supply thereof. <Amended on Jun. 28, 2016>
  (2) The supply of land, facilities, etc. under paragraph (1) shall be made by lottery at a price determined in advance by the implementer; provided, the land, facilities, etc. to be used for sale, such as a superstore, specialized shopping complex, etc. (excluding cases where land, facilities, etc. necessary for livelihood measures are supplied in lieu of land, facilities, etc. in consideration of the status of ownership of the original land, etc. of residents and their livelihood, etc.) shall be supplied by competitive bidding. <Amended on Jan. 5, 2021>
  (3) Where an implementer intends to supply land, facilities, etc. pursuant to paragraph (2), he or she shall publicly announce the following matters; provided, the foregoing shall not apply where a person to be supplied is specified or his or her eligibility is restricted, if he or she has given individual notice:
  1. The name and address of the implementer and the name of the representative;
  2. Location, area, and use of land, facilities, etc. (including restrictions on the use of land, facilities, etc., if any);
  3. Methods and conditions of supply;
  4. Supply prices or methods of determining them;
  5. Qualification requirements for persons to be supplied and methods of selection;
  6. The period and place of application for supply;
  7. Other matters deemed necessary by the implementer.
  (4) Notwithstanding paragraph (2), an implementer may supply land, facilities, etc. by means of a negotiated contract in any of the following cases. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Feb. 2, 2012; Mar. 23, 2013>
  1. Where a site for public facilities that cannot be sold to the general public, such as school sites, sites for public office buildings, etc., is supplied to the State, a local government, or any other person eligible to install the relevant public facilities pursuant to relevant statutes or regulations
  2. Where minimum land necessary for the maintenance and management of facilities to be retained in accordance with an implementation plan publicly notified pursuant to Article 29(1) of the Act is supplied;
  3. Where land is supplied to a person who has transferred all of the land, etc. owned by him or her in a logistics complex to the project implementer in accordance with the standards prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport in response to consultation under the Act on Acquisition of and Compensation for Land, etc. for Public Works Projects;
  4. Where land is redeemed according to land redemption bonds;
  5. Where it is deemed inevitable to supply land with adjacent landowners, etc., the utility value of which is substantially low in light of the scale, shape, location conditions, etc. of the land, and the supply of such land to adjacent landowners, etc.;
  6. Where an implementer falling under Article 27(2)1 through 3 of the Act supplies land to a person selected in accordance with the procedures and methods prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport because it is necessary to develop a logistics complex in a complex and three-dimensional manner for the development of the logistics industry;
  6-2. Where a site for logistics facilities (excluding sales facilities) to be directly used by an enterprise included in a plan for the placement of types of business to be invited, among the matters publicly notified pursuant to Article 23(1) of the Act, is supplied to such enterprise after consultation with the authority designating logistics complexes;
  7. Where it is permitted to supply products under a negotiated contract pursuant to the relevant statutes or regulations.
  (5) Other matters necessary for the methods, etc. of supplying land, facilities, etc. shall be prescribed by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Mar. 23, 2013>

Article 42 (Transfer of land, facilities subject to restriction on disposal) (1) Where any occupant enterprise or support institution intends to transfer the land, facilities, etc. sold in lots to an implementer or a management agency referred to in Article 53 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "management agency") before completing the installation of logistics complex facilities or support facilities pursuant to Article 51(1) of the Act, it shall submit an application for disposal to the implementer or the management agency, along with documents prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Mar. 23, 2013>
  (2) Upon receipt of an application for disposition under paragraph (1), an implementer or a management agency shall select a person to be transferred pursuant to Article 51(1) of the Act and notify the applicant for disposition thereof within the period prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport from the date of receipt of the application for disposition. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Mar. 23, 2013>
  (3) Where an implementer or a management agency intends to select a person to be transferred pursuant to paragraph (2), it shall publicly announce the following matters in advance and receive an application for purchase from an applicant for occupancy: <Amended on Jan. 5, 2021>
  1. Indication of the goods for sale;
  2. Selling price and method of payment;
  3. Timing of purchase;
  4. Qualifications for occupancy of the purchaser;
  5. Other matters required by the implementer or management agency.
  (4) Other persons prescribed by Presidential Decree in Article 51(1)3 of the Act means the following institutions: <Amended on Nov. 20, 2009; Jan. 6, 2012; Mar. 24, 2014; May 31, 2016; Oct. 25, 2016; Apr. 2, 2019; Feb. 17, 2022>
  1. Technology guarantee under the Korea Technology Finance Corporation Act;
  2. Technology guarantee under the Korea Technology Finance Corporation Act;
  3. The Korea Asset Management Corporation established under the Act on the Establishment of Korea Asset Management Corporation;
  4. The NongHyup Bank established under the Agricultural Cooperatives Act;
  5. The Suhyup Bank established under the Fisheries Cooperatives Act;
  6. The National Forestry Cooperatives Federation established under the Forestry Cooperatives Act;
  7. The Korea Federation of Small and Medium Business established under the Small and Medium Enterprise Cooperatives Act;
  8. The Korea SMEs and Startups Agency under the Small and Medium Enterprises Promotion Act;
  9. A local government-invested public corporation established under the Local Public Enterprises Act for the purpose of land development projects;
  10. An institution that an operator or a management institution deems particularly necessary to manage the relevant logistics complex.
  (5) "Interest and Expenses prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 51(2) of the Act means the following amounts. <Amended on Sep. 20, 2010>
  1. The amount calculated by multiplying the acquisition price of land, facilities, etc. to be transferred by the producer price index during the period from the date of acquisition to the date of transfer;
  2. Acquisition tax and other taxes and public charges incurred in purchase; provided, it shall not be included in the calculation of taxes collected due to reasons attributable to the acquirer;
  3. Expenses incurred in maintaining, preserving or improving the land, facilities, etc. to be transferred.
  (6) Where a person referred to in any subparagraph of Article 51(1) of the Act intends to transfer the land, facilities, etc. purchased pursuant to that paragraph, he or she shall consult with the management agency in advance.
  (7) The transfer price of land, facilities, etc. purchased by a person referred to in any subparagraph of Article 51(1) of the Act pursuant to the same paragraph may be the aggregate of interest and expenses referred to in any subparagraph of paragraph (5) to the acquisition price.

Article 42-2 (Classification of logistics complex renewal projects) (1) Where a project for the complete renovation of a logistics complex under Article 52-2(2) of the Act is accompanied by an alteration of a land use plan and a plan for major infrastructure under Article 22(5)5 of the Act (including an amendment to a building plan and a complex site use plan under the proviso to Article 22-2(3) of the Act), which involves rearrangement (including phased rearrangement) of at least 50/100 of the area of the designated logistics complex. <Amended on Jun. 28, 2016>
  (2) A partial renovation project of a logistics complex under Article 52-2(2) of the Act means a logistics complex renewal project other than those referred to in paragraph (1).
  (3) "Minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the latter part of Article 52-2(3) of the Act means matters other than the subparagraphs of Article 13(2).
  (4) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 52-2(4)8 of the Act means the following:
  1. Period for implementing the logistics complex renovation project;
  2. A plan to expand support facilities;
  3. Data on surveys on the demand for occupancy;
  4. Details of land, etc., if any, and the owner thereof, and the name and address of a relevant person defined in subparagraph 5 Article 2 of the Act on Acquisition of and Compensation for Land for Public Works Projects.
  (5) "Minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the latter part of Article 52-2(5) of the Act means matters under the subparagraphs of Article 22(3).
  [This Article Added on Aug. 11, 2010]

Article 42-3 (Public notice of designation, approval, or authorization) Matters to be publicly notified pursuant to Article 52-3(2) of the Act shall be as follows:
  1. The name of a project;
  2. The name and address of the implementer (in cases of a corporation, its name and the name of its representative);
  3. The location and area of the proejct area;
  4. Details of and grounds for the disposition;
  [This Article Added on Aug. 11, 2010]

Article 43 (Scope of management organization) "A management body prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 53(1) of the Act means any of the following persons: <Amended on Jun. 28, 2016>
  1. The Korea Land and Housing Corporation incorporated under the Korea Land and Housing Corporation Act;
  2. The Korea Expressway Corporation under the Korea Expressway Corporation Act;
  3. The Korea Water Resources Corporation under the Korea Water Resources Corporation Act;
  4. The Korea Rural Community Corporation under the Korea Rural Community Corporation and Farmland Management Fund Act;
  5. The Port Authority under the Port Authority Act;
  6. Local government-invested public corporations prescribed in the Local Public Enterprises Act.
  [This Article Added on Feb. 2, 2012]
  [Moving from Article 43-2; Previous Article 43 to Article 43-2 <Jun. 28, 2016>]

Article 43-2 (Composition and operation of consultative council of tenant enterprises) (1) The council of tenant enterprises under Article 53(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "council of tenant enterprises") shall be comprised of at least 75 percent of tenant enterprises of the relevant logistics complex at the time of its organization. <Amended on Feb. 8, 2010; Feb. 2, 2012>
  (2) The council of tenant enterprises shall be comprised of general members and special members.
  (3) The general members of the council of tenant enterprises shall be representatives of the tenant enterprises, and special members shall be determined from among persons other than general members, and the membership qualifications shall be governed by the articles of incorporation of the council of tenant enterprises. <Amended on Feb. 2, 2012>
  (4) The council of tenant enterprises shall hold an ordinary general meeting of occupant enterprises within two months from the commencement date of each business year and may hold an extraordinary general meeting, if necessary.
  (5) Except as otherwise provided for in the articles of incorporation, a resolution of a meeting of the council of tenant enterprises shall require the attendance of a majority of the members and the concurring vote of a majority of the members present.
  [Moving from Article 43; Previous Article 43-2 to Article 43 <Jun. 28, 2016>]

Article 44 (Details of management guidelines for logistics complexes) Each logistics complex management plan under Article 54(1) of the Act shall include descriptions of the following matters:
  1. Matters concerning the formulation of a logistics complex management plan under Article 55 of the Act;
  2. Matters concerning the types of business to be invited by logistics complexes and standards therefor;
  3. Matters necessary for the management of a logistics complex, such as maintenance, repair, and improvement of sites and facilities of the logistics complex.

Article 45 Deleted. <Aug. 11, 2010>

Article 46 (Collection of joint charges) (1) "Other common facilities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 56(2) of the Act means the following facilities : <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Mar. 23, 2013>
  1. Roads in the complex;
  2. Facilities for preventing water pollution;
  3. Other facilities prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.
  (2) A management agency shall collect joint contributions for public facilities pursuant to Article 56(2) of the Act according to the degree of profits accruing from the use of public facilities by tenant enterprises and support institutions; provided, where it is impracticable to calculate the degree of profits, the entire expenses shall be collected according to the burden ratio calculated according to the area of the site, the total floor area of construction, and the number of employees of the tenant enterprises and support institutions.
  (3) A management agency may collect joint charges every month or quarterly according to the operational status of the logistics complex.

CHAPTER IV-2 MAINTENANCE PROJECTS FOR LOGISTICS TRAFFIC AND ENVIRONMENT

Article 46-2 (Requirements for designation of maintenance district of logistics traffic and environment) (1) Areas for which an application for designation of a maintenance district of logistics traffic and environment may be filed pursuant to Article 59-4(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "improvement district") shall be an area that meets all of the following requirements:
  1. Areas where it is necessary to improve infrastructure, such as construction, expansion, improvement, repair, etc. of roads or to improve living environment, such as prevention of noise and vibration and reduction of fine dust, due to concentration of logistics facilities;
  2. The area of the area to be designated as a maintenance district shall be at least 300,000 square meters;
  3. The total site area of the logistics facilities shall be at least 30/100 of the area of the area to be designated as a maintenance district.
  (2) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 59-4(2)6 of the Act means the following:
  1. Matters concerning the systematic development, maintenance, etc. of logistics facilities;
  2. Expected effects of the maintenance project in traffic and environment improvement;
  3. Matters concerning the formulation or modification of an urban or Gun management plan under the National Land Planning and Utilization Act
  4. Other matters requested by a Mayor/Do Governor to be included, as deemed necessary for the maintenance of logistics traffic and environment., by the Mayor/Do Governor.
  [This Article Added on Dec. 10, 2020]

Article 46-3 (Hearing opinions of residents) (1) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu intends to make it available for residents' public inspection under the main clause of Article 59-4(3) of the Act, he or she shall publicly announce the following matters on the website or daily newspapers in advance:
  1. Outline of the maintenance district;
  2. Period and place for perusal of the draft maintenance plan;
  3. Timing and methods of presenting opinions.
  (2) Residents of an area subject to improvement districts may present their opinions to the head of a Si/Gun/Gu during the period from the date of commencement of perusal under Article 59-4(3) of the Act to the date seven days after the expiration of the period for perusal.
  (3) The head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall hold a briefing session for residents under Article 59-6(2) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "briefing session for residents") within the period for perusal, and where an area subject to a maintenance district extends over at least two jurisdictions of Sis/Guns/Gus, the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall hold a briefing session for residents in each Si/Gun/Gu.
  [This Article Added on Dec. 10, 2020]

Article 46-4 (Alteration of minor matters) "Any alteration of minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso of Article 59-4(3) of the Act means any of the following:
  1. Alteration of the area of the relevant maintenance district or less than 5/100 of the maintenance project costs;
  2. Revision of calculation errors, typos, omissions or other obvious errors equivalent thereto.
  [This Article Added on Dec. 10, 2020]

Article 46-5 (Composition and operation of joint committee) (1) Pursuant to Article 59-5(1) of the Act, a Mayor/Do Governor shall organize a joint committee to have a logistics complex planning deliberation committee established under Article 59-2 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "logistics complex planning deliberation committee") and a local urban planning committee established under Article 113 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act (hereinafter referred to as "local urban planning committee") jointly deliberate on the designation of a maintenance district.
  (2) The Joint Committee under paragraph (1) shall be organized in accordance with the following standards:
  1. Members of the Joint Committee, excluding the chairperson, shall be appointed or commissioned by the Mayor/Do Governor from among the members of the committee for deliberation on logistics complex plans and the local urban planning committee;
  2. The number of members of the Joint Committee shall not exceed 25 persons;
  3. The number of members of the committee for deliberation on logistics complex plans shall be at least 1/2 of the members of the Joint Committee.
  (3) The chairperson of the Joint Committee shall be the Vice Mayor designated by the Mayor in cases of the Special Metropolitan City, Metropolitan City, or Special Self-Governing City, and the Vice Governor designated by the Governor in cases of a Do or Special Self-Governing Province.
  [This Article Added on Dec. 10, 2020]

Article 46-6 (Public notice of designation of maintenance districts) Public notice under Article 59-5(3) of the Act shall include the following matters:
  1. Outline of the relevant maintenance plan, such as the location and area of the relevant maintenance district and the period of maintenance;
  2. The current status of a maintenance district (the number of population, the number and area of logistics facilities, traffic volume, and the cargo traffic volume);
  3. A infrastructure maintenance plan, including construction, expansion, improvement, and repair of a road;
  4. A plan for the improvement of living environments, such as the prevention of noise and vibration and the reduction of fine dust;
  5. A cost-sharing plan for a maintenance project;
  6. Expected effects of the maintenance project in traffic and environment improvement;
  7. Matters concerning the systematic development, maintenance, etc. of logistics facilities in a maintenance district;
  8. Matters concerning the formulation or modification of an urban or Gun management plan under the National Land Planning and Utilization Act;
  9. Other matters deemed necessary to be publicly notified by a Mayor/Do Governor.
  [This Article Added on Dec. 10, 2020]

Article 46-7 (Cancellation of designation of maintenance districts) (1) When a Mayor/Do Governor intends to cancel the designation of a maintenance district pursuant to Article 59-6(1) of the Act, he or she shall hear opinions of the head of the competent Si/Gun/Gu before jointly deliberating on the designation of the logistics complex planning deliberation committee and the local urban planning committee.
  (2) Article 46-5 shall apply mutatis mutandis to the deliberation on the cancellation of designation of a maintenance district under Article 59-6(1) of the Act and Article 46-3 to the methods, etc. of explanatory meetings for residents, perusal by residents, and hearing opinions of residents under Article 59-6(2) of the Act, respectively.
  (3) Public notice under Article 59-6(3) of the Act shall include the following matters:
  1. Outline of the relevant maintenance plan, such as the location and area of the relevant maintenance district and the period of maintenance;
  2. The current status of the relevant maintenance district (including matters changed compared with those at the time of filing an application for designation of the maintenance district);
  3. Grounds for canceling a maintenance district;
  4. Other matters deemed necessary to be publicly notified by a Mayor/Do Governor.
  [This Article Added on Dec. 10, 2020]

Article 46-8 (Support for maintenance projects for logistics traffic and environment) "Projects prescribed by Presidential Decree" in subparagraph 4 of Article 59-7 of the Act means projects for installing, maintaining, or improving charging facilities for electric vehicles defined in subparagraph 3 of Article 2 of the Act on Promotion of Development and Distribution of Environment-Friendly Motor Vehicles and hydrogen-fuel supply facilities defined in subparagraph 9 of that Article.
  [This Article Added on Dec. 10, 2020]

